Not that there's anything wrong with what Dan has said, but it appears from
this and other recent posts that some clarification is in order.

Quest artifacts are specific to a character class, eg the PYEC is specific to
tourists etc. They also have an alignment (Lawfull, Neutral, or Chaotic)
which is gained from this. So the PYEC, for example, is neutral because
tourists are neutral.

If you wish, or otherwise aquire, a quest artifact that is not proper to your
class, then you get blasted for HP as DAN has already said. In addition if the
artifact is of a different alignment (eg., a Knight (lawfull) trying to pick
up the PYEC) then the artifact is also repulsed, and drops to the floor again.

So while picking up a quest artifact of the wrong class may cost you some HP,
picking up one of the wrong alignment will get you nowhere.

